body:
Good question, that is ancient code.

I think it is better we remove that comment as it is hard to keep such random comments in sync when things change.
These are the kind of things that should be looked up on the `GodotShape3D::get_data()` functions for each shape.

I still looked at the PhysicsServer `GodotHeightMapShape3D` and it returns a Dictionary with ...

```
Dictionary d;
d["width"] = width;
d["depth"] = depth;

const AABB &shape_aabb = get_aabb();
d["min_height"] = shape_aabb.position.y;
d["max_height"] = shape_aabb.position.y + shape_aabb.size.y;

d["heights"] = heights;
```

So it is still somehow correct but ignores the `min_height` and `max_height` keys.

